hadiths[28]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1869","On the authority of Al-Aghar Al-Muzani, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “It is a burden on my heart, and I ask forgiveness from Allah a hundred times a day” [Muslim]."
"1870","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying, “By Allah, I seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him more than seventy times a day” [Al-Bukhari]."
"1871","And on his authority, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you had not sinned, Allah Almighty would have taken you away and brought a people who would sin and seek forgiveness from Allah Almighty and He would forgive them” [Muslim]."
"1872","We counted Messenger's saying a hundred times during one single sitting: Rabb- ighfir li, wa tubb 'alayya, innaka Antat-Tawwabur-Rahim. (My Rubb! Forgive me and pardon me. Indeed, You are the Oft-Returning with compassion and Ever Merciful.\ [Abu Dawud and At- Tirmidhi] ."""
"1873","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever persists in seeking forgiveness, Allah will make for him a way out of every distress and a relief from every worry, and will provide for him from where he did not expect.” [Abu Dawud]"
"1874","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \He who says: 'Astaghfir ullah-alladhi la ilaha illa Huwal-Haiyul-Qayyumu"," wa atubu ilaihi (I seek the forgiveness of Allah"," there is no true god except Allah"," the Ever-Living"," the Self- Subsisting"," and I turn to Him in repentance)","' his sins will be forgiven even if he should have run away from the battlefield (while he was engaged in fighting for the Cause of Allah).\"" [Abu Dawud"," At-Tirmidhi and Al-Hakim (on conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim for accepting Hadith)] ."""
"1875","On the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “The master of seeking forgiveness is for the servant to say: Oh Allah, You are my Lord, there is no god but You, You created me and I am Your servant, and I abide by Your covenant and promise as much as I can. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge Your blessings upon me, and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for no one forgives sins except You. Whoever said it during the day, being certain of it, died on that day.” Before the evening, he is one of the people of Paradise, and whoever says it during the night while being certain of it and dies before the morning, he is one of the people of Paradise” [Al-Bukhari]. (1)"
"1876","Whenever the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) finished his Salat (prayer), he would beg forgiveness three times [by saying, 'Astaghfirullah' (3 times)] and then he would say: \Allahumma Antas-Salamu"," wa minkas-Salamu"," tabarakta ya Dhal-Jalali wal-Ikram. (O Allah! You are the Bestower of security and security comes from You; Blessed are You. O Possessor of glory and honour).\"" Imam Al-Auza'i (one of the subnarrators) of this Hadith was asked: \""How forgiveness should be sought?\"" He replied: \""I say: Astaghfirullah"," Astaghfirullah (I seek forgiveness from Allah. I seek forgiveness from Allah).\"" [Muslim] ."""
"1877","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to often say before his death: “Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him. I seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1878","I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying, \Allah"," the Exalted"," has said: 'O son of Adam! I shall go on forgiving you so long as you pray to Me and aspire for My forgiveness whatever may be your sins. O son of Adam! I do not care even if your sins should pile up to the sky and should you beg pardon of Me"," I would forgive you. O son of Adam! If you come to Me with an earthful of sins and meet Me"," not associating anything with Me in worship"," I will certainly grant you as much pardon as will fill the earth.\""' [At-Tirmidhi] ."""
"1879","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, \O women folk! You should give charity and be diligent in seeking Allah's forgiveness because I have seen (i.e."," on the Night of the Ascension to the highest heavens) that dwellers of the Hell are women.\"" A woman amongst them said: \""Why is it that the majority of the dwellers of Hell are women?\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) replied"," \""You curse frequently and are ungrateful to your husbands. You are the most deficient in intellect and religion among people.\"" Upon this the woman asked: \""What is the deficiency in our wisdom and in our religion?\"" He (ﷺ) replied"," \""Your lack of wisdom can be well judged from the fact that the evidence of two women is equal to that one man. Your not offering Salat (prayer) for some days is a deficiency in religion.\"" [Muslim] ."""
"1880","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The people of Paradise will eat therein and drink, and will not defecate, blow their nose, or urinate, but their food is belch like musk. They are inspired to glorify and magnify Allah, just as they are inspired to breathe.” [Muslim]"
"1881","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah Almighty said: I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no thought has occurred to the heart of man. And recite, if you wish: {And not a soul shall know what is hidden for them of comfort to their eyes as a recompense for what they used to do} [Al-Sajdah: 17] [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1882","On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The first group to enter Paradise will be in the form of the moon on the night of the full moon, then those who follow them will be like the brightest, most radiant star in the sky. They will not urinate, defecate, spit, or blow their nose. Their combs will be gold, their scent will be musk, and their censers will be aloe - the perfumed stick. Their wives will be virgins, with the creation of one man, in the image of their father Adam, sixty cubits in Heaven” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration by Al-Bukhari and Muslim: Their vessels contain gold, and they are exuded with musk, and each one of them has two wives whose beauty can be seen from the marrow of their leg behind the flesh. There is no disagreement between them, nor hatred. Their hearts are the heart of one man. They glorify Allah morning and evening. His saying: (On the creation of one man). Some of them narrated it with fatha al-kha and sukkan al-lam, and some of them narrated it with a dhammah with both of them, and both of them are authentic."
"1883","On the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said: “Moses (ﷺ) asked his Lord, ‘Who is the lowest in status to the people of Paradise?’ He said: He is a man who comes after the people of Paradise have been admitted to Paradise, and it is said to him: Enter Paradise. He says: ‘O Lord, how can you, when the people have descended into their places and taken what they deserve?’ So He says to him: ‘Would you be satisfied to have a king like a king from The kings of the world? So he says: I am satisfied with my Lord. He says: You have that and like it and like it and like it and like it and like it. Then he says on the fifth: I am satisfied, O Lord. He says: This is for you and ten times the same, and for you is whatever your soul desires and your eyes are pleased with. So he says: I am satisfied with my Lord. He said, “My Lord, who has the highest status among them?” He said: “Those whose dignity I planted with my hand and sealed it, but no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and it has not occurred to a human heart.” [Muslim]"
"1884","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \I know of the last of the inhabitants of the Hell to be taken out from there and the last one to enter Jannah. He is a man who will come out of the Fire"," crawling on all fours. Allah"," the Rubb of glory and honour will say to him: 'Go and enter Jannah.' He will go to it and think that it is full up. He will then come back and say: 'O my Rubb"," it is full up.' Allah will say to him: 'Go and enter Jannah.' He will again go to it and think that it is full up. So he will turn back. Allah will again say: 'Go and enter Jannah. For you have what is equal to ten times the world.' He will say: 'Are You making fun of me while You are the King?\"" At this I (i.e."," the narrator) saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) laugh till his premolars were visible and he said"," \""Such man will be the last dweller of Jannah in its lowest rank.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"1885","On the authority of Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “The believer in Paradise will have a tent made of a single, hollow pearl, sixty miles long in the sky, and the believer will have family in it. The believer will walk around them, so they will not see each other. (Agreed upon).” A mile: six thousand cubits."
"1886","On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Indeed, in Paradise there is a tree under which a rider, a swift, lean horse, will travel for a hundred years without crossing it” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. It was also narrated in the two Sahihs, also from the narration of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: “A rider will travel in its shade for a year without crossing it."
"1887","On the authority of him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “The people of Paradise will see the people of the chambers above them just as you would see the shining star setting on the horizon from the east or the west, to differentiate between them.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, are these the stations of the prophets that no one else can reach? He said: “Yes, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, there are men who believed in Allah and were truthful to the messengers” ((Agreed upon). On him).."
"1888","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \A space in Jannah equal to the span of a bow will be better than all that upon which the sun rises and sets.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"1889","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \In Jannah there is a market to which the people will come every Friday. The northern wind will blow and shower fragrance on their faces and clothes and"," consequently"," it will enhance their beauty and loveliness. They will then return to their wives who will also have increased in their beauty and loveliness"," and their families will say to them: 'We swear by Allah that you have been increased in beauty and loveliness since leaving us.' Thereupon they will reply: 'We swear by Allah that you have also been increased in beauty and loveliness since we left you.\""' [Muslim] ."""
"1890","On the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The people of Paradise will see the rooms in Paradise as you see the star in the sky” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1891","And on his authority, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I witnessed a session with the Prophet (ﷺ) in which he described Paradise until he finished, then he said at the end of his hadith: “In it is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no thought has occurred to the heart of man.” Then he recited “Their sides will turn away from their beds” until the Almighty’s saying: “So no soul knows what is hidden for them of the comfort of eyes.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"1892","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \When the dwellers of Jannah enter Jannah"," an announcer will call: (You have a promise from Allah that) you will live therein and you will never die; you will stay healthy therein and you will never fall ill; you will stay young and you will never become old; you will be under a constant bliss and you will never feel miserable.\"" [Muslim] ."""
"1893","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The lowest place for one of you in Paradise is to be told to him: Make a wish, and he makes a wish and wishes. He says to him: Did you make a wish? He says: Yes, and he says to him: For you have what you wished for and the like of it with it” [Muslim]."
"1894","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," will say to the inhabitants of Jannah: 'O inhabitants of Jannah!' They will respond: 'Here we are! At Your service"," O our Rubb. All good is in Your Hand!' He will ask them: 'Are you pleased?' They will reply: 'Why should we not be pleased"," O Rubb"," when You have given us what You have not given to any of Your creatures?' Allah will say: 'Shall I not give you something better than that?' They will ask: 'O Rubb! What can be better than that?' Allah will say: 'I shall bestow My Pleasure upon you and I shall never be displeased with you.\""' [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"1895","We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when he looked at the full moon and observed, \You shall see your Rubb in the Hereafter as you are seeing this moon; and you will not feel the slightest inconvenience in seeing Him.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"1896","I called on the Prophet (ﷺ) with two of my cousins. One of them said to him: ""O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), appoint me governor of some land over which Allah has given you authority."" The other also requested for something of the same nature. Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""By Allah we do not appoint someone to this post who seeks it or someone who contends for it.""

."," Allah"," the Glorious and Exalted"," will say to them: 'Do you wish me to give you anything more?' They will reply: 'Have You not made our faces bright? Have You not brought us into Jannah and delivered us from the Hell?' And Allah will remove the Veil. The (dwellers of Jannah) will feel that they have not been awarded anything dearer to them than looking at their Rubb.\"" [Muslim] . Allah"," the Exalted"," says: \""Verily"," those who believe and do deeds of righteousness"," their Rubb will guide them through their Faith; under them will flow rivers in the Gardens of Delight (Jannah). Their way of request therein will be Subhanaka Allahumma (Glory to You"," O Allah!) and Salam (peace"," safety from evil) will be their greetings therein (Jannah)! and the close of their request will be: Al-hamdu lillahi Rabbil-'Alamin [All the praises and thanks are to Allah"," the Rubb of 'Alamin (mankind"," jinn and all that exists)] .\"" (10:9","10)"""
